 line]\n.ard/332/logs/worker-engineer-20261124T184913.498Z.log:8:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/332/logs/worker-engineer-20261124T184913.498Z.log:25:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/332/plan.md:8:   - `PatchID(ctx, repoDir, from, to, path string) (string, error)`: run `git diff --no-ext-diff --no-textconv --no-renames <from> <to> -- <path>` (use the `GIT_ATTR_SOURCE=emptyTree` and `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` env that `CodeChanged` uses), pipe it via the `stdin` argument of `g.run` into `git patch-id --stable`, and return the first field. An empty diff or empty output is an error (fail closed). Wrap errors like the neighbours do.\n.ard/332/plan.md:9:2. `internal/prgate/prgate.go`: widen the `Git` interface with `MergeBase`, `Parents` and `PatchID` (`*gitx.Git` already satisfies it). Update the fake in `prgate_test.go` and any other implementer of `prgate.Git` (grep `prgate.Git`, `CodeChanged(` in tests of `internal/merger` and `internal/reviewer`).\n.ard/332/plan.md:10:3. `internal/prgate/prgate.go`: add `CoversDetail(ctx, g, repoDir, reviewed, head, base string, issue int) (Cover, error)` where new `type Cover struct { OK bool; Broken, PatchEqual []string }`, and make `Covers` a thin wrapper returning `(c.OK, c.Broken, err)` so the reviewer's mark-ready caller (`internal/reviewer/ready.go:86`, `base \"\"`) is unchanged. In `CoversDetail`, after the existing loop computes `broken` (only when `base != \"\"`), if `broken` is non-empty run the new rule:\n.ard/332/plan.md:13:   - For each path in `broken`: `a = PatchID(oldBase, reviewed, p)`, `b = PatchID(newBase, head, p)`. Equal ids: the path goes to `PatchEqual`. Otherwise it stays in `Broken`. Any error returns `Cover{}` and the error.\n.ard/332/plan.md:16:4. `internal/merger/merge.go:89` (review gate): call `prgate.CoversDetail`; when `PatchEqual` is non-empty log `t.log.Info(\"merge.cover_patch_equal\", \"pr\", n, \"issue\", issue, \"role\", role, \"reviewed\", reviewed, \"head\", head, \"paths\", strings.Join(PatchEqual, \",\"))`. Keep `paths=len(Broken)` in `merge.reviews_stale`. Same at `:228` in `hasApproval` (log with the approval commit `at`); keep the \"not comparable on error\" behaviour there.\n.ard/332/plan.md:26:- `TestCoversPatchGitError`: fake whose `PatchID` fails, and one whose `MergeBase` or `Parents` fails. Expect not OK and the error returned.\n.ard/332/plan.md:30:- `internal/gitx`: `PatchID` equal for the same change at shifted line offsets, differs for a changed line, errors on a bad rev.\n.ard/332/review-eng-review.md:12:      firstUpdateMerge still has no test for a two-parent head whose first-parent chain misses the reviewed commit, nor for the maxChain cap.\n.ard/332/review-eng-review.md:15:The patch-id cover rule matches the issue and plan, fails closed on git errors and on changed patches, and the merger wiring and docs are updated. Approved; the one earlier non-blocking test gap is still open.\n.ard/332/triage-engineer.md:6:Adds a patch-id comparison to the shared head-cover check so a path changed by both the PR and main stays covered when the PR's own patch to it is unchanged after a clean update-branch merge. It wires the rule into the merger's review gate and approval check, logs the covered paths, and updates the proposal. The plan has five steps with real-repo tests for each acceptance case. Size M, risk medium because it loosens a security-relevant gate.\n.ard/332/triage-lead.md:11:- triage:engineer: implementation steps for the patch-id comparison in the prgate package, wiring into the merger's review gate and protected-path approval check, the new log event, gittest-based tests for each acceptance case, and the proposal's merger section.\n.ard/332/worker-engineer.md:9:- `internal/gitx/inspect.go`: `Parents` and `PatchID` helpers (fail closed).\n.ard/332/worker-engineer.md:10:- `internal/prgate/prgate.go`: `CoversDetail` with the patch-id rule, applied only when the head is reached from the reviewed commit through two-parent update-branch merges; `Covers` is a wrapper, so mark-ready and reviewfix landing are unchanged.\n.ard/332/worker-engineer.md:11:- `internal/merger/merge.go`: the review gate and approval check use `CoversDetail` and log `merge.cover_patch_equal`.\n.ard/346/logs/triage-engineer-20261124T231555.701Z.log:25:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/366/logs/triage-lead-20261124T234720.310Z.log:5:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/366/logs/triage-lead-20261124T234720.310Z.log:9:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/366/logs/triage-lead-20261124T234720.310Z.log:10:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/366/logs/triage-lead-20261124T234720.310Z.log:11:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/366/logs/triage-lead-20261124T234720.310Z.log:12:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/366/logs/triage-lead-20261124T234720.310Z.log:13:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/366/logs/triage-lead-20261124T234720.310Z.log:14:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/366/triage-lead.md:15:- The issue leaves two choices open, and the plan should settle them. First, whether to raise ard's minimum git version or only fail closed when merge-tree write-tree support is missing. Second, whether to replace the patch-id comparison or keep it next to the new merge check.\ninternal/gitx/inspect.go:99:// PatchID returns the stable patch id (git patch-id --stable) of the change to\ninternal/gitx/inspect.go:102:func (g *Git) PatchID(ctx context.Context, repoDir, from, to, path string) (string, error) {\ninternal/gitx/inspect.go:111:\tout, _, err := g.run(ctx, repoDir, nil, diff, nil, \"--git-dir=\"+gitDirOf(repoDir), \"patch-id\", \"--stable\")\ninternal/gitx/inspect.go:113:\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"gitx: patch-id: %w\", err)\ninternal/gitx/inspect.go:117:\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"gitx: patch-id %.12s %.12s %s: no output\", from, to, path)\ninternal/gitx/inspect_test.go:473:func TestPatchIDAndParents(t *testing.T) {\ninternal/gitx/inspect_test.go:504:\ta, err := g.PatchID(ctx, dir, c1, c2, \"f.txt\")\ninternal/gitx/inspect_test.go:508:\tif b, err := g.PatchID(ctx, dir, c1, c2, \"f.txt\"); err != nil || a != b {\ninternal/gitx/inspect_test.go:511:\tif b, err := g.PatchID(ctx, dir, c3, c4, \"f.txt\"); err != nil || a == b {\ninternal/gitx/inspect_test.go:514:\tif b, err := g.PatchID(ctx, dir, c4, c5, \"f.txt\"); err != nil || a == b {\ninternal/gitx/inspect_test.go:517:\tif _, err := g.PatchID(ctx, dir, c1, c1, \"f.txt\"); err == nil {\ninternal/gitx/inspect_test.go:520:\tif _, err := g.PatchID(ctx, dir, c1, \"nope\", \"f.txt\"); err == nil {\ninternal/merger/loop.go:69:\tPatchID(ctx context.Context, repoDir, from, to, path string) (string, error)\ninternal/merger/merge.go:91:\t\tcov, err := prgate.CoversDetail(ctx, d.Git, d.RepoDir, reviewed, head, base, issue)\ninternal/merger/merge.go:234:\t\t\tcov, err := prgate.CoversDetail(ctx, d.Git, d.RepoDir, at, head, base, issue)\ninternal/prgate/prgate.go:110:// PatchGit is the part of *gitx.Git CoversDetail adds to Git.\ninternal/prgate/prgate.go:115:\tPatchID(ctx context.Context, repoDir, from, to, path string) (string, error)\ninternal/prgate/prgate.go:118:// Cover is the outcome of CoversDetail.\ninternal/prgate/prgate.go:125:// CoversDetail is Covers with one more rule for base != \"\": a path both the PR\ninternal/prgate/prgate.go:130:func CoversDetail(ctx context.Context, g PatchGit, repoDir, reviewed, head, base string, issue int) (Cover, error) {\ninternal/prgate/prgate.go:137:// firstUpdateMerge walks first parents from head to reviewed. It returns the\ninternal/prgate/prgate.go:140:func firstUpdateMerge(ctx context.Context, g PatchGit, repoDir, reviewed, head string) (string, error) {\ninternal/prgate/prgate.go:193:\tsecond, err := firstUpdateMerge(ctx, pg, repoDir, reviewed, head)\ninternal/prgate/prgate.go:206:\t\ta, err := pg.PatchID(ctx, repoDir, oldBase, reviewed, p)\ninternal/prgate/prgate.go:210:\t\tb, err := pg.PatchID(ctx, repoDir, base, head, p)\ninternal/prgate/prgate_test.go:301:\treturn CoversDetail(context.Background(), gitx.New(\"\"), r.dir, reviewed, head, base, 1)\ninternal/prgate/prgate_test.go:370:func (g errPatchGit) PatchID(context.Context, string, string, string, string) (string, error) {\ninternal/prgate/prgate_test.go:386:\t\tc, err := CoversDetail(context.Background(), g, \"\", \"rev\", \"head\", \"base\", 1)\ninternal/prgate/prgate_test.go:398:\tc, err := CoversDetail(context.Background(), errPatchGit{Git: fg, patchErr: boom}, \"\", \"rev\", \"head\", \"\", 1)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c71e5ff3-7cd6-4100-ad39-01ec3e8e4a0d","uuid":"1cece31a-1ea9-4964-8173-95aecbb143bf","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:02:26.140Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":".ard-input/366/comments.md:17:- The issue leaves two choices open, and the plan should settle them. First, whether to raise ard's minimum git version or only fail closed when merge-tree write-tree support is missing. Second, whether to replace the patch-id comparison or keep it next to the new merge check.\n.ard-input/366/issue.md:15:#332 (PR 356, merged) lets a review or approval keep covering a PR after an update-branch merge when the PR's own change to each file both sides touched has the same `git patch-id --stable`. Two gaps (found in the security review of #323):\n.ard-input/366/issue.md:17:1. **Whitespace and moves.** `PatchID` (`internal/gitx/inspect.go`) uses `git patch-id --stable`, which ignores whitespace and line numbers. A merge that changes behaviour through whitespace alone (Python or YAML indentation, Makefile tabs) or moves a hunk keeps the same patch id.\n.ard-input/366/issue.md:18:2. **Any merge counts.** `firstUpdateMerge` (`internal/prgate/prgate.go`) accepts any two-parent merge whose first parent is the reviewed head. A hand-crafted merge pushed to a PR branch by someone with push access (and, once #323 lands, a merge ard's worker authors in a conflict round) has exactly that shape.\n.ard-input/366/issue.md:20:Together they let a stale **human protected-path approval** stay valid (`internal/merger/merge.go`, the approval check uses `CoversDetail`), not only AI review labels. The proposal's sentence \"a conflict resolution ... changes the patch and breaks the cover\" is not true for whitespace.\n.ard-input/366/issue.md:24:- In `firstUpdateMerge`, count a merge as an update merge only if its tree **equals a clean mechanical merge of its parents**: `git merge-tree --write-tree <p1> <p2>` with no conflicts and the same tree id. Run it with the hardened config (empty `GIT_ATTR_SOURCE`, no rerere, no renormalize). `merge-tree --write-tree` needs git 2.38+; raise ard's minimum git, or fail closed (not covered) when it is unavailable.\n.ard-input/366/issue.md:25:- And/or make the comparison whitespace-exact: replace `patch-id --stable` with a hash of the raw diff (`--no-ext-diff --no-textconv --no-renames`, full context lines), so whitespace and moves change it.\n.ard/293/logs/triage-lead-20261124T193353.460Z.log:10:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/299/logs/triage-lead-20261124T184528.651Z.log:8:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/300/logs/triage-lead-20261124T184528.570Z.log:8:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/307/logs/triage-lead-20261124T193353.402Z.log:10:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/323/logs/triage-engineer-20261124T204827.328Z.log:24:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/323/logs/triage-engineer-20261124T213318.768Z.log:7:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/323/logs/triage-engineer-20261124T213318.768Z.log:18:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/323/logs/triage-engineer-20261124T213318.768Z.log:19:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/332/logs/review-eng-review-20261124T184040.945Z.log:4:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/332/logs/review-eng-review-20261124T184040.945Z.log:7:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/332/logs/review-eng-review-20261124T184040.945Z.log:14:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/332/logs/review-eng-review-20261124T184040.945Z.log:16:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/332/logs/review-eng-review-20261124T184040.9